1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:02,920
( giggling )

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,339
ARE YOU LOOKING AT
NAKED TRIBESWOMEN?

3
00:00:05,339 --> 00:00:07,967
NO. LOOK.

4
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,302
THAT'S A PIG.

5
00:00:10,302 --> 00:00:13,263
I KNOW, I KNOW, BUT LOOK
AT THE KNOBS ON IT.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,852
HEY.

7
00:00:17,852 --> 00:00:19,144
HEY.
HEY.

8
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,938
EMILY'S COUSIN
KICKED ME OUT.

9
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:22,481
WHAT?
WHY?

10
00:00:22,481 --> 00:00:24,483
WELL, WHEN YOU'RE SUBLETTING
AN APARTMENT

11
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:27,026
FROM YOUR WIFE'S COUSIN,
AND THEN YOU GET A DIVORCE

12
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:29,864
SOMETIMES THE COUSIN SUDDENLY
WANTS HIS APARTMENT BACK.

13
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:31,490
DIDN'T YOU
SIGN A LEASE?

14
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:34,159
WHO NEEDS A LEASE
WHEN IT'S FAMILY?

15
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:37,705
HEY, YOU COULD
STAY WITH US.

16
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:38,706
WE'LL TAKE
CARE OF YOU.

17
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:40,290
ANYTHING
YOU NEED, MAN

18
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,959
BUT YOU HAVE TO PROMISE ME
YOU WILL LET US KNOW

19
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:43,418
THE SECOND YOU ARE
FEELING BETTER

20
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:47,006
SO WE CAN MAKE FUN
OF YOUR HAIR.
YEAH.

21
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,340
YOU GOT IT.

22
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,842
OKAY.

23
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:51,802
THANKS, YOU GUYS,
I REALLY APPRECIATE THIS.

24
00:00:51,802 --> 00:00:54,013
I'M GOING TO GET PACKING AGAIN.

25
00:00:54,013 --> 00:00:56,139
I'VE BEEN MOVING AROUND
SO MUCH LATELY

26
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,850
I'M BEGINNING
TO FEEL LIKE A NOMAD.

27
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:00,477
( giggling )

28
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:01,478
WHAT?

29
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,898
HE THOUGHT YOU SAID "GONAD."

30
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:16,243
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

31
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:18,453
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

32
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:21,540
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

33
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:26,085
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

34
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:28,881
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

35
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:30,883
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

36
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:34,553
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,638
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

38
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:39,433
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

39
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:41,518
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

40
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:44,688
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

41
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:48,025
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

42
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:59,453
IF EVERY RESTAURANT
WERE AS CLEAN AS YOURS

43
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:01,371
IT'D BE A TOUGH TIME
MAKING A LIVING.

44
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:03,498
OH, LARRY.

45
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:05,793
SO, UM, DO HEALTH INSPECTORS
WORK ON COMMISSION?

46
00:02:05,793 --> 00:02:07,377
NO. BRIBES.

47
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,254
IT'S OKAY TO LAUGH, RIGHT?

48
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:11,799
YEAH. I WAS JUST KIDDING.
OKAY.

49
00:02:11,799 --> 00:02:13,425
I'M GOING TO CHECK
THE KITCHEN FLOOR.

50
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:14,885
OKAY. KNOCK YOURSELF OUT, LARRY.

51
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:18,388
YUMMY.

52
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,599
WHAT? LARRY?

53
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:21,934
OH, YEAH. I'D LET HIM

54
00:02:21,934 --> 00:02:23,477
CHECK OUT MY
KITCHEN FLOOR.

55
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:28,607
A 98.

56
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,275
I DEDUCTED
TWO POINTS BECAUSE

57
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,485
YOU'RE NOT WEARING
YOUR CHEF'S HAT

58
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:34,446
AND THAT IS
A SECTION FIVE VIOLATION.

59
00:02:34,446 --> 00:02:36,197
LOOK, LARRY, HONEY

60
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:39,451
UM... I WROTE THE BOOK
ON SECTION FIVE

61
00:02:39,451 --> 00:02:41,202
AND I KNOW THAT
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO WEAR YOUR HAT

62
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:42,370
UNLESS YOU'RE
IN THE KITCHEN.

63
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,831
WHERE IS YOUR HAT?

64
00:02:43,831 --> 00:02:45,290
IT'S IN THE KITCHEN.
I'LL GO GET IT.

65
00:02:46,834 --> 00:02:48,085
THERE'S THE TWO POINTS.

66
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:52,589
HEY, YOU SHOULD REALLY READ
THAT BOOK YOU WROTE.

67
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,763
WOW.

68
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,431
YOU SAW THE HAT
IN THE KITCHEN

69
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,100
AND YOU KNEW
SHE'D HAVE TO GO

70
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,893
IN THERE HATLESS
TO GET IT.

71
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,478
YOU COULD HAVE
YOUR OWN, YOU KNOW

72
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:08,605
HEALTH INSPECTOR
DETECTIVE SHOW.

73
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:11,108
WELL, I DON'T
KNOW ABOUT THAT.

74
00:03:11,108 --> 00:03:14,611
YEAH, BUT THEN I COULD BE YOUR
SIDEKICK, VUNDA.

75
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:16,530
MAYBE VUNDA COULD
GIVE ME HER NUMBER

76
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,197
AND I COULD ASK HER
TO DINNER SOMETIME.

77
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:20,701
OKAY, SHE WOULD LOVE THAT,
YOU KNOW

78
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:24,997
SINCE YOU KNOW
ALL THE CLEAN PLACES TO EAT.

79
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:26,414
I'LL CALL YOU.

80
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,708
OKAY.

81
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:34,715
HE'S SO FUNNY. WHOA. OH.

82
00:03:41,096 --> 00:03:43,098
THANK YOU.

83
00:03:43,098 --> 00:03:44,432
MON, HOW'S ROSS DOING

84
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:47,144
YOU KNOW, SINCE
ALL THE EMILY STUFF?

85
00:03:47,144 --> 00:03:48,645
HE'S NOT GREAT,
BUT, UM...

86
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:50,189
HE'S DEALING WITH IT.
OH.

87
00:03:50,189 --> 00:03:51,899
OH, WAIT A MINUTE,
YOU'RE NOT GOING TO...?

88
00:03:51,899 --> 00:03:53,441
OH, HONEY, PLEASE, NO.

89
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:55,694
I CAN'T GET STARTED WITH
ALL THAT ROSS STUFF AGAIN.

90
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:58,238
HE'S GOING TO BE
SCREWED UP FOR A LONG TIME.

91
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,781
AND BESIDES, YOU KNOW

92
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:02,492
I DON'T GO FOR GUYS
RIGHT AFTER THEY GET DIVORCED.

93
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:03,869
RIGHT. YOU ONLY
GO FOR THEM

94
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,704
FIVE MINUTES BEFORE
THEY GET MARRIED.

95
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,753
TWO POUNDS OF MOCHA JAVA,
PLEASE.

96
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:14,088
IT'S DANNY.

97
00:04:14,088 --> 00:04:15,380
ARE YOU GUYS EVER
GOING OUT AGAIN?

98
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,132
I DON'T KNOW.
HE HASN'T CALLED ME

99
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:18,842
SINCE THAT ONE TIME
WE WENT OUT.

100
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,719
I SEE HIM IN THE HALLWAY,
WE FLIRT.

101
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:22,763
I'M ALL...
( insincere laughing )

102
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:24,848
...AND NOTHING.

103
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:25,849
HEY.

104
00:04:25,849 --> 00:04:26,892
HI, DANNY.

105
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:28,518
WOW. THIRSTY, HUH?

106
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,771
ACTUALLY, I'M HAVING A
PARTY AT MY PLACE ON SATURDAY--

107
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:32,106
SORT OF A HOUSEWARMING THING.

108
00:04:32,106 --> 00:04:33,857
OH, FUN.
OH, GREAT.

109
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:35,734
I'M REALLY LOOKING
FORWARD TO IT.

110
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:36,860
OKAY, SEE YOU.

111
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,534
WELL, I GUESS WE WON'T
BE WARMING HIS HOUSE.

112
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,704
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

113
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,998
I SEE WHAT HE'S DOING.

114
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:51,208
HE'S NOT ASKING ME OUT

115
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:54,253
BECAUSE HE WANTS ME
TO ASK HIM OUT.

116
00:04:54,253 --> 00:04:55,587
YOU'RE NOT
GOING TO DO THAT?

117
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:56,838
THAT'S RIGHT.

118
00:04:56,838 --> 00:05:00,717
BECAUSE THAT WOULD
GIVE HIM THE CONTROL.

119
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:02,301
SO NOW HE'S ALL,
OOH, COMING UP WITH THIS

120
00:05:02,301 --> 00:05:03,386
"I'VE GOT A PARTY" THING--

121
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:04,846
YOU KNOW,
TRYING TO GET ME

122
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,974
TO HINT AROUND
FOR AN INVITATION.

123
00:05:06,974 --> 00:05:08,892
BLEW UP IN HIS FACE,
DIDN'T IT?

124
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:11,061
SO THERE
IS NO PARTY?

125
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:12,729
OH, NO.

126
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,355
THERE'S A PARTY.

127
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:17,776
THERE'S A PARTY,
BUT THE POWER--

128
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:20,403
THAT IS STILL UP FOR GRABS.

129
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,239
YOU FOLLOW ME?

130
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:23,657
I THINK SO.

131
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:26,409
SO HE'S NOT INVITING
YOU TO HIS PARTY

132
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:27,953
BECAUSE HE LIKES YOU.

133
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,329
EXACTLY.

134
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,090
ROSS?

135
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,633
HEY, ROOMIES.

136
00:05:41,633 --> 00:05:43,093
HEY.

137
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:45,720
LOVE WHAT YOU'VE DONE
WITH THE PLACE.

138
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,640
YEAH, I KNOW, I KNOW,
IT'S A LOT OF BOXES

139
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,476
BUT AGAIN, I REALLY APPRECIATE
YOU GUYS LETTING ME STAY HERE.

140
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:52,811
NOT A PROBLEM.

141
00:05:52,811 --> 00:05:55,105
AND SINCE YOU'LL
BE HERE A WHILE

142
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:58,317
I WAS THINKING WE'D PUT YOUR
NAME ON THE ANSWERING MACHINE.

143
00:05:58,317 --> 00:06:01,028
OH. I, UH, HOPE YOU DON'T MIND

144
00:06:01,028 --> 00:06:04,531
BUT I KIND OF ALREADY
JAZZED IT UP A LITTLE.

145
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,158
CHECK IT OUT.

146
00:06:06,158 --> 00:06:11,038
( playing intro to
"We Will Rock You" )

147
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:16,293
Ross:
♪ We will, we will
call you back. ♪

148
00:06:16,293 --> 00:06:17,294
HEY.

149
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:18,503
ALL RIGHT.

150
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,088
PRETTY COOL, HUH?

151
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:24,551
YOU'RE FAKE LAUGHING,
TOO, RIGHT?

152
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:26,427
OH, THE TEARS ARE REAL.

153
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:32,517
YOU LOOK BEAUTIFUL
THIS EVENING.

154
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,602
SHOW ME THE BADGE AGAIN.

155
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:42,361
SHINY.

156
00:06:42,361 --> 00:06:43,362
YOU MIND IF I WASH UP?

157
00:06:43,362 --> 00:06:44,863
I CAME STRAIGHT FROM WORK

158
00:06:44,863 --> 00:06:46,614
AND WHO KNOWS WHERE
THESE BABIES HAVE BEEN?

159
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,867
YOU ARE JUST NON-STOP.

160
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:00,337
WE'RE OUT OF HERE.

161
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,504
WHY?

162
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,714
JUST WALKING
PAST THE KITCHEN

163
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:04,091
I SAW TEN VIOLATIONS.

164
00:07:04,091 --> 00:07:05,675
I AM SHUTTING
THIS PLACE DOWN.

165
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,344
YOU HAVE THE POWER TO DO THAT?

166
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:09,470
THIS DOES.

167
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,973
SHUT IT DOWN.

168
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:24,403
HEY.

169
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,822
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

170
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:31,492
NOTHING.

171
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,036
YOU BUILT A FORT, DIDN'T YOU?

172
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:37,374
KIND OF.

173
00:07:37,374 --> 00:07:39,584
OH, MY GOD, THE AIR PURIFIER.

174
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,086
ROSS'S AIR PURIFIER.

175
00:07:41,086 --> 00:07:43,380
ALL I HEARD FOR FOUR YEARS
THROUGH COLLEGE WAS...

176
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:46,091
( humming )

177
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:48,718
YOU SHOULD HAVE GONE OUT
ONCE IN A WHILE.

178
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,387
I HATE THIS THING.

179
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:52,139
COME ON, CHANDLER.

180
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,140
ROSS IS OUR FRIEND.

181
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,808
HE NEEDS US RIGHT NOW.

182
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:58,353
WHY DON'T YOU BE A GROWNUP
AND COME WATCH TV IN THE FORT?

183
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:03,858
( knocking on door )

184
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:04,943
OH, HI, DANNY.

185
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,611
I JUST WANTED
TO INVITE YOU

186
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:07,821
TO THE PARTY
TOMORROW NIGHT.

187
00:08:07,821 --> 00:08:09,239
OH, THANKS.

188
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:10,740
I'LL TRY TO
STOP BY.

189
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,701
YEAH, ACTUALLY, I THINK...
I'M GOING TO BE BUSY.

190
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:14,828
YOU ARE?

191
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,579
YEAH. REMEMBER?

192
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:19,124
I'VE GOT THAT,
UH... GALA.

193
00:08:20,459 --> 00:08:22,710
WHAT'S THE GALA FOR?

194
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,296
UH, IT'S A, UM...

195
00:08:24,296 --> 00:08:26,798
IT'S A, IT'S A
REGATTA GALA.

196
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:28,758
REALLY? YOU SAIL?

197
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:31,803
NO. NO, BUT I SUPPORT IT.

198
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:35,098
OKAY. WELL, HOPE I SEE YOU
TOMORROW NIGHT.

199
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:36,183
OKAY.
TAKE CARE.

200
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:38,059
OKAY.

201
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:43,315
WALKED RIGHT INTO THAT ONE,
DIDN'T HE?

202
00:08:43,315 --> 00:08:44,441
WHAT ONE?

203
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:46,193
YOU WANTED HIM
TO INVITE YOU

204
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:47,652
TO THE PARTY AND HE DID.

205
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:49,654
YEAH, BUT HE WAITED
UNTIL THE LAST MINUTE.

206
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:51,072
SO IF I SAID YES,
HE WOULD KNOW

207
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:53,158
I HAD NOTHING BETTER
TO DO THAN WAIT AROUND

208
00:08:53,158 --> 00:08:54,993
FOR AN INVITATION
TO HIS STUPID PARTY.

209
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:56,495
I SAID NO,
WHICH PUTS ME

210
00:08:56,495 --> 00:09:00,665
RIGHT BACK IN
THE DRIVER'S SEAT.

211
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,167
SO, THE BALL IS IN
HIS COURT?

212
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,377
BALL?

213
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:05,462
NO, THERE'S NO BALL.

214
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:10,342
( rhythmic slapping )

215
00:09:16,431 --> 00:09:17,932
JOEY, PLEASE.

216
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,017
SORRY.

217
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:25,023
( rattling )

218
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:30,820
( shrieking )

219
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:37,077
HELLO, CHILDREN.

220
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,370
HEY.

221
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:39,829
WANT TO PLAY SOME FOOSBALL?

222
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,540
PLEASE?

223
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,083
OKAY.

224
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,418
NO, NO. NO.

225
00:09:44,418 --> 00:09:46,711
WE HAD TO MOVE THE TABLE
INTO MY ROOM

226
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,755
BECAUSE OF ALL THE BOXES.

227
00:09:48,755 --> 00:09:50,173
COME ON.

228
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:57,722
ALL RIGHT, I
HAVE ONE QUESTION.

229
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:01,226
WHAT IS THE DEAL WITH THIS?

230
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:04,729
BYE-BYE, LITTLE PUPPET-JOEY
HAND?

231
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,981
NO, NO, THE "QUIET DOWN" THING.

232
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,568
OH, YOU MEAN THIS.

233
00:10:09,568 --> 00:10:12,112
MM! MM!

234
00:10:12,112 --> 00:10:15,115
I DON'T KNOW HOW
MUCH MORE I CAN TAKE.

235
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,742
DID YOU KNOW HE TAPED OVER
MY BAYWATCH TAPE

236
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,369
WITH SOME SHOW ABOUT BUGS?

237
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,456
MY GOD.

238
00:10:22,456 --> 00:10:24,165
WHAT IF THAT HAD BEEN PORN, HUH?

239
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,544
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, YOU KNOW

240
00:10:27,544 --> 00:10:28,920
THIS MAY BE TOUGH,
BUT COME ON, IT'S ROSS.

241
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,964
I SURVIVED COLLEGE WITH HIM.

242
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:34,134
ALL RIGHT. I GUESS I CAN
HOLD OUT A LITTLE LONGER.

243
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,343
LET'S HAVE A GAME.

244
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,303
OKAY.

245
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,473
NO, NO, NO.

246
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:40,681
YES!

247
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:42,476
( laughing )

248
00:10:42,476 --> 00:10:44,018
UH, FELLAS?

249
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:50,275
( door closes )

250
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:52,444
OKAY, SO HE'S OUT OF HERE.

251
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:01,161
YOU GUYS GOT ANYTHING TO EAT?

252
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,579
I JUST WENT
DOWN TO JOHN-O's

253
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:04,247
FOR SOME CHICKEN,
AND IT WAS CLOSED.

254
00:11:04,247 --> 00:11:06,791
I TOOK LARRY THERE TO EAT,
BUT IT WAS ALL VIOLATED

255
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,876
SO WE SHUT IT DOWN.

256
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:11,254
PHEEBS, IF THIS GUY
KEEPS CLOSING DOWN

257
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:14,007
ALL OUR FAVORITE PLACES,
WHERE WE GOING TO EAT?

258
00:11:14,007 --> 00:11:15,758
I DON'T KNOW;
CLEAN PLACES?

259
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,260
MMM. YUM.

260
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,220
( knocking on door )

261
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:24,392
IT'S DANNY.

262
00:11:24,392 --> 00:11:26,727
DON'T LET HIM IN. I'M SUPPOSED
TO BE AT A REGATTA GALA.

263
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:28,146
WE'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

264
00:11:28,146 --> 00:11:30,273
CAN'T YOU JUST SAY IT
STARTS LATER?

265
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:34,110
WHAT KIND OF A REGATTA GALA
STARTS AT NIGHT?

266
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:35,820
THE FAKE KIND.

267
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:41,576
HEY, UM, I NEED A LADLE.

268
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:42,577
YOU GOT A LADLE?

269
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:43,662
WE HAVE A LADLE.

270
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:46,998
THANKS. SEE YOU
AT THE PARTY.

271
00:11:46,998 --> 00:11:48,166
OKAY. GREAT.

272
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:50,627
HEY, YOU GUYS.

273
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:51,961
YOU KNOW WHAT LARRY WOULD SAY?

274
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,963
HE'D SAY, "SEE YOU LADLE."

275
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:58,343
( Phoebe laughing )

276
00:11:58,343 --> 00:12:00,345
WELL, I'M DONE WITH THIS.
YOU WANT ANYTHING, ROSS?

277
00:12:00,345 --> 00:12:01,929
UH, SPORTS?
INTERNATIONAL?

278
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,223
APARTMENT LISTINGS?

279
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:05,058
UH, I'LL TAKE SPORTS.

280
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,976
MINE.

281
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:08,228
ALL RIGHT.

282
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,896
UH, INTERNATIONAL.

283
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:11,105
THAT'S MINE, TOO.

284
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:14,859
I'M ITALIAN.

285
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:18,238
I GUESS I COULD CHECK OUT
THOSE APARTMENT LISTINGS

286
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:20,823
EVEN THOUGH THERE'S
NEVER ANYTHING IN HERE.

287
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,617
NOT EVEN ON PAGE SEVEN?

288
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,580
OH, YEAH. YOU'RE RIGHT.

289
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:28,582
OH, HERE'S AN AFFORDABLE PLACE.

290
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:31,000
TWO BEDROOM, CLOSE TO WORK.

291
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,503
OOH, IT'S AVAILABLE
IN FIVE WEEKS.

292
00:12:33,503 --> 00:12:35,672
WHAT ABOUT THAT
CIRCLED ONE?

293
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,340
OH, I DON'T KNOW.

294
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:40,343
IT'S KIND OF EXPENSIVE
FOR A STUDIO.

295
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:41,760
BUT IT'S AVAILABLE NOW...

296
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,680
ISN'T IT?

297
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,348
YES, IT IS.

298
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:48,017
LET'S GO
LOOK AT IT.

299
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,603
OKAY, LET'S GO.

300
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:50,978
HERE WE GO.
HEY, HEY.

301
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:52,355
OH, OH, OH,
HEY, GUYS.

302
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:54,524
I WAS WONDERING
IF YOU WOULD, UH...

303
00:12:54,524 --> 00:12:57,026
MAYBE CHIP IN FOR
SOME NEW AIR FILTERS

304
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:58,570
FOR THE PURIFIER?

305
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:01,281
I MEAN, AFTER ALL,
WE ARE ALL USING IT.

306
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:02,657
LET'S GO QUICKER.

307
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:14,001
( long, appreciative whistle)

308
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,255
OH, MY GOD.

309
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:18,256
MMM.

310
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:19,549
LOOK AT
THIS KITCHEN...

311
00:13:19,549 --> 00:13:22,719
SLASH BATHROOM.

312
00:13:22,719 --> 00:13:23,844
THAT'S GREAT, YOU KNOW

313
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:25,722
SO YOU CAN COOK
WHILE IN THE TUB.

314
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:28,391
SOMEBODY WAS
USING HIS HEAD.

315
00:13:30,143 --> 00:13:32,019
HEY, LET'S CHECK OUT
THE REST OF THE PLACE.

316
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:43,698
I THINK THIS IS IT.

317
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:45,032
I DON'T KNOW.

318
00:13:45,032 --> 00:13:47,118
MAYBE WE SHOULD
KEEP LOOKING.

319
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:50,705
BUT, HEY, ROSS, THIS
PLACE IS AVAILABLE NOW.

320
00:13:50,705 --> 00:13:51,830
YOU DON'T WANT
TO BE STUCK WITH US

321
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,873
FOR THE NEXT
FIVE WEEKS.
YEAH.

322
00:13:59,714 --> 00:14:01,716
SO YOU THINK
I SHOULD GO AHEAD

323
00:14:01,716 --> 00:14:03,092
AND TAKE THIS PLACE?

324
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,219
IT'S PERFECT.

325
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,432
HOW ABOUT YOU?

326
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:13,186
KITCHEN SLASH BATHROOM.

327
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,107
UH, I SEE WHAT
YOU GUYS ARE SAYING.

328
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,900
I'LL, UH... I'LL
GO DOWNSTAIRS

329
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,944
FILL OUT AN APPLICATION.

330
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:28,618
WE ARE BAD PEOPLE.

331
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:31,120
HE KNEW WE WERE TRYING
TO GET RID OF HIM.

332
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,747
HE KNEW.

333
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:37,001
YOU THINK WE COULD GET
A BATHTUB IN OUR KITCHEN?

334
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,717
HEY, YOU READY FOR DINNER?

335
00:14:43,717 --> 00:14:44,801
OOH, ABSOLUTELY.

336
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:45,926
GREAT.

337
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,136
YOU WANT THE ITALIAN PLACE

338
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,304
DOWN ON BLEECKER, RIGHT?

339
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,390
OOH, I LOVE THAT PLACE.

340
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:52,600
SO... NO.

341
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,519
OH, HOW ABOUT
MAMA LEZOTTI'S?

342
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:56,020
UGH.

343
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,856
SURE.

344
00:14:57,856 --> 00:15:00,650
I WONDER HOW LONG THAT
MILK HAS BEEN SITTING OUT.

345
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,735
OH, NO. THIS PLACE

346
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:03,194
IS TOTALLY HEALTHY.

347
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:04,987
THIS MILK IS MINE.

348
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:09,325
I BOUGHT THIS TODAY BECAUSE I
WAS THIRSTY FOR MILK, YOU KNOW.

349
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:15,331
OKAY, LET'S GO.

350
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:19,919
HEY, BUDDY.

351
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,170
YOU FAMILIAR WITH
SECTION 11-B

352
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,463
OF THE HEALTH CODE

353
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,048
THAT REQUIRES
ALL REFUSE MATERIAL

354
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:25,592
TO BE TAKEN OUT
OF THE BACK EXIT?

355
00:15:25,592 --> 00:15:26,925
BUT THEN I HAVE TO GO

356
00:15:26,925 --> 00:15:28,261
ALL THE WAY
AROUND THE DRY CLEANER.

357
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:29,929
OH, SO YOU'RE
SAYING YOU CHOOSE

358
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:31,431
CONVENIENCE
OVER HEALTH?

359
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:33,892
OKAY, STOP.
LARRY...

360
00:15:33,892 --> 00:15:36,853
OKAY, CAN'T
YOU JUST BE LARRY

361
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:39,689
AND NOT LARRY THE
HEALTH INSPECTOR GUY?

362
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:41,524
YOU KNOW, I MEAN, IT
WAS REALLY EXCITING

363
00:15:41,524 --> 00:15:43,693
AT FIRST, BUT NOW,
IT'S LIKE, OKAY--

364
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:47,238
SO WHERE ARE WE
GOING TO EAT EVER?

365
00:15:47,238 --> 00:15:48,865
WELL, I SUPPOSE
I COULD

366
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,784
GIVE HIM A WARNING.

367
00:15:50,784 --> 00:15:52,118
THANK YOU.

368
00:15:52,118 --> 00:15:53,745
OKAY, GO,
GO, GO.

369
00:15:57,749 --> 00:15:59,250
NOW, IF, AFTER DINNER

370
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,586
YOU STILL, LIKE, REALLY
NEED TO BUST SOMEONE

371
00:16:01,586 --> 00:16:04,130
I KNOW A HOT-DOG VENDOR
WHO PICKS HIS NOSE.

372
00:16:08,593 --> 00:16:10,887
MAYBE... MAYBE WE
DID A GOOD THING

373
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,179
HELPING ROSS GET
BACK ON HIS FEET.

374
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:14,808
YES, THAT WAS
A NICE PLACE.
YEAH.

375
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:16,183
NOT A LOT OF
CLOSET SPACE

376
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:17,811
BUT HE COULD JUST
HANG HIS STUFF

377
00:16:17,811 --> 00:16:20,521
OUT THE WINDOW
IN A BAG.
YEAH.

378
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:25,401
WHAT WILL WE DO?

379
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:27,445
I DON'T KNOW.

380
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:29,238
MAYBE PIZZA?

381
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:31,616
ABOUT ROSS.

382
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:32,784
OH.

383
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:35,369
( telephone ringing )

384
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:39,081
HELLO?

385
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:41,542
OH, YEAH.

386
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,085
IT'S THE APARTMENT MANAGER.

387
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:45,463
ROSS PUT US DOWN
AS REFERENCES.

388
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:48,132
ROSS IS THE GREATEST
GUY YOU'LL EVER MEET.

389
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:49,676
YEAH, HE'S
VERY RELIABLE.

390
00:16:49,676 --> 00:16:51,552
OF COURSE, HE HAS
A BIG, HUGE DOG

391
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,471
THAT, UH, BARKS INTO THE NIGHT.

392
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:57,183
WELL, WHO DOESN'T LOVE DOGS?

393
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,227
UH, HE'S A TAP DANCER.

394
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:04,315
YES, SOME WOULD SAY
THAT IS A LOST ART.

395
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:06,609
HE'S A PIMP.

396
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,989
THERE YOU GO.
YES, HE'S A PIMP.

397
00:17:10,989 --> 00:17:13,115
HE'S A BIG, TAP DANCING PIMP.

398
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:15,451
HELLO?

399
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:28,464
OH.

400
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,768
THIS IS NEVER
GOING TO WORK.

401
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:41,978
HE'S RIGHT THERE.

402
00:17:41,978 --> 00:17:43,855
JUST GO OVER
AND SAY HI.

403
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:46,357
I HAVE TO GO DOWNSTAIRS,
COME BACK UP

404
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:49,027
AS IF I'M COMING HOME
FROM THE REGATTA GALA.

405
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:50,862
OKAY? SO JUST
GO DISTRACT HIM

406
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:51,988
BUT DON'T BE SEXY.

407
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:56,034
HEY, DANNY.

408
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:57,702
WHAT'S GOING ON?

409
00:17:57,702 --> 00:17:59,328
IT'S A GREAT PARTY.

410
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,538
GREAT FOOD.

411
00:18:00,538 --> 00:18:01,789
UH-HUH.

412
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,374
YOU KNOW,
MOST PARTIES--

413
00:18:03,374 --> 00:18:08,046
IT'S ALL CHIPS AND
SALSA, CHIPS AND SALSA.

414
00:18:08,046 --> 00:18:10,297
SO, UH...

415
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:11,883
WHAT'S THIS?

416
00:18:11,883 --> 00:18:13,760
SALAD.

417
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,553
OH.

418
00:18:15,553 --> 00:18:18,138
AND, UH,
WHAT'S THIS?

419
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:20,391
BREAD.

420
00:18:20,391 --> 00:18:22,852
AREN'T YOU A CHEF?

421
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:25,730
OH.

422
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,065
HEY, RACHEL.

423
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:29,358
HEY. OH, RIGHT.

424
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,235
TONIGHT WAS YOUR PARTY.

425
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:33,571
YOU LOOK GREAT.
I'M GLAD YOU COULD MAKE IT.

426
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:37,324
OH, YEAH, WELL, YOU KNOW,
THE GALA HAD TO END SOMETIME.

427
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:38,618
DON'T GO ANYWHERE.

428
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:40,078
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK,
ALL RIGHT?

429
00:18:40,078 --> 00:18:41,203
YEAH, SURE.

430
00:18:43,039 --> 00:18:45,750
ALL RIGHT, WHOSE COURT'S
THE BALL IN NOW?

431
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:47,919
I THOUGHT THERE
WASN'T A BALL.

432
00:18:47,919 --> 00:18:50,463
OH, COME ON.

433
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:52,130
HE'S GLAD THAT I CAME.

434
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:54,133
HE DOESN'T WANT ME
TO GO ANYWHERE.

435
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:56,427
BALLS FLYING ALL
OVER THE PLACE.

436
00:18:57,887 --> 00:18:59,764
RACHEL, THIS IS
MY FRIEND, TOM.

437
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:02,600
THIS IS THE GIRL
I TOLD YOU ABOUT.

438
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,979
OH, COME ON, YOU'RE
TELLING PEOPLE ABOUT ME?

439
00:19:05,979 --> 00:19:07,730
I THINK YOU TWO COULD
REALLY HIT IT OFF.

440
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,357
I'M GOING
TO GO MINGLE.

441
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:14,612
SO, YOU WORK
AT BLOOMINGDALE'S, HUH?

442
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:17,323
MY MOM CALLS IT "BLOOMIES."

443
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:23,412
OH... YEAH.

444
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,999
OKAY. AT EASE, SOLDIER.

445
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:28,876
I'M SORRY?

446
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,003
IT'S ALL RIGHT.

447
00:19:30,003 --> 00:19:31,129
YOU CAN JUST
DROP THE ACT, TOMMY.

448
00:19:31,129 --> 00:19:32,546
I KNOW WHAT'S
GOING ON HERE.

449
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:34,799
YOU'RE DANNY'S
WINGMAN, RIGHT?

450
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:36,092
YOU GUYS ARE BEST BUDS.

451
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:37,384
FRAT BROS.

452
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:42,515
I'M GOING TO GO TALK
TO A FRIEND.

453
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:45,685
YEAH, YEAH. YOU GO
TALK TO YOUR FRIEND.

454
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,770
YOU GO TELL HIM,
"NICE TRY."

455
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:55,277
MAN, YOU KNOW, HE JUST KEEPS
LOBBING THEM UP AND I JUST KEEP

456
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:57,446
KNOCKING THEM RIGHT
OUT OF THE PARK.

457
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,616
I THINK I NEED A DRINK.

458
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:01,742
YEAH.

459
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:09,458
98... 99...

460
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:11,794
ONE... HUNDRED.

461
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:13,337
OKAY. GO.

462
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:15,089
DUDE, I'M TELLING YOU, I'M FINE.

463
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:21,387
HERE WE GO, HERE WE GO.

464
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:22,930
HEY.

465
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,473
HEY.

466
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:27,143
SO, I, UH... I DIDN'T
GET THAT APARTMENT.

467
00:20:27,143 --> 00:20:29,269
SOME PROBLEM
WITH MY APPLICATION.

468
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:31,147
Both:
YOU'RE KIDDING!

469
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:32,606
YEAH, BUT THE
GOOD NEWS IS

470
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:33,858
PHOEBE SAID
I COULD STAY

471
00:20:33,858 --> 00:20:35,526
AT HER PLACE FOR A WHILE, SO...

472
00:20:35,526 --> 00:20:37,403
WELL, YOU CAN'T STAY
WITH PHOEBE, ROSS.

473
00:20:37,403 --> 00:20:38,738
WE'RE ROOMIES.

474
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:40,406
LOOK, YOU GUYS
DON'T NEED ME HERE

475
00:20:40,406 --> 00:20:41,741
TAKING UP ALL YOUR SPACE.

476
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:43,450
WE GOT PLENTY
OF SPACE.

477
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:46,453
THERE'S STILL SOME OVER
THERE BY THAT SPEAKER.

478
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,581
PLEASE, JUST STAY.

479
00:20:48,581 --> 00:20:50,666
YEAH.

480
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,001
ARE YOU GUYS
SURE ABOUT THIS?

481
00:20:52,001 --> 00:20:53,211
DEFINITELY, YES.

482
00:20:53,211 --> 00:20:55,295
YES. ROSS,
YOU HAVE TO STAY.

483
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,464
ALL RIGHT.

484
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:58,799
ALL RIGHT,
BUDDY.

485
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,676
HEY.

486
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,720
SO I'M A PIMP, HUH?

487
00:21:05,181 --> 00:21:07,307
IT'S OKAY.

488
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:10,228
LOOK, I KNOW SOMETIMES
I CAN BE A PAIN IN THE ASS

489
00:21:10,228 --> 00:21:11,645
BUT YOU JUST HAVE
TO TALK TO ME.

490
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:14,732
TELL ME IF SOMETHING'S
BOTHERING YOU, OKAY?

491
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:17,610
AND FOR MY PART,
I'LL REALLY DO EVERYTHING I CAN

492
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:20,196
TO KEEP MY ANNOYING HABITS
YOU KNOW, JUST...

493
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:39,215
WELL, I SEE YOU'VE HAD
A VERY PRODUCTIVE DAY.

